    "pin": {
      "title": "Les Espaces d'Abraxas",
      "description": "Building complex in Noisy-le-Grand, France",
      "extract": "Les Espaces d'Abraxas is a high-density housing complex in Noisy-le-Grand, approximately 12 km (7.5 mi) from Paris, France. The building was designed by architect Ricardo Bofill and his architecture practice Ricardo Bofill Taller de Arquitectura (RBTA) in 1978 on behalf of the French government, during a period of increased urbanisation across France after World War II. This rapid urbanisation led to overcrowding and insufficient housing in Paris. To offset this, the French government implemented a project to create five 'New Towns' on the outskirts of the city.",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Espaces_d'Abraxas",
      "coordinates": {
        "lat": 48.8401,
